      "value": "@{5bcbaf75fab2337b72ced6b0|full_name}: You're both missing the point and also wrong at the same time. The point is to allow PC users to see the Quest version of avatars and worlds instead of the PC version.\nThe part you're wrong regarding is with how worlds work. Same as avatars, a cross platform world can be uploaded for each platform with considerable differences. They share the same world ID, but are distinct scenes. It's possible to upload a quest world, and then make a graphically and feature enhanced version for PC, with both existing as the same instance.\nFurther any world uploaded only for Quest can only be entered by Quest users. All worlds must be uploaded for both (using the same ID) in order to be cross platform.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
